{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityEditingGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistedAssociations","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"],"title":"Keys","anchor":"Keys"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"],"title":"Protocol","anchor":"Protocol"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"],"title":"Implementations","anchor":"Implementations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"KeyValueStore","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a small protocol for one-shot scalar values that don’t fit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" model. Three implementations ship:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" — production, backed by any ","type":"text"},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" suite","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" — production, backed by the system Keychain (survives reinstall)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" — tests, dictionary-backed, reference semantics","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject through your "},{"code":"Environment","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", hydrate state at startup, and write from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects. Reducers stay pure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public protocol KeyValueStore: Sendable {","    func value<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Value?","    @discardableResult","    func setValue<Value>(_ value: Value?, for key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","    @discardableResult","    func removeValue<Value>(for key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","    func contains<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All values are JSON-encoded as "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Reads and writes go through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which pairs a backing-store name with its "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value type at compile time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"When to Use What","anchor":"When-to-Use-What","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Need","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Collection of identifiable entities (decks, cards, sessions)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Scalar preference (theme, sort order, last-seen version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (UserDefaults)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Anonymous device identity that must survive reinstall","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (Keychain)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Last-known-good entitlement cache (offline pro gate)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (Keychain) — backs "},{"code":"ResilientPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is for many-of-a-kind data with change tracking and batched"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes. ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is for one-of-a-kind values that you read once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"startup and overwrite on change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"UserDefaults vs Keychain","anchor":"UserDefaults-vs-Keychain","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Survives reinstall?","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes (this-device-only by default)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Backup \/ device migration","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Included","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Excluded with default accessibility","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Throughput","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Fast (in-memory cache)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Slower (system call)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Visible to other apps?"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No (per app\/group)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Optionally (App Groups via ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessGroup:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Best for"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Theme, sort order, feature toggles, last-seen version"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Anonymous device ID, opaque tokens, last-known-good entitlement","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Keychain costs more per access — hydrate once at launch and observe state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"afterward, never read inside a reducer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer the Keychain for anything a user could gain by forging it. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last-known-good entitlement cache is the clearest case: it grants pro offline,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":" plist (editable directly or via a doctored-backup restore)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lets a spoofed value unlock the app. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"persists that cache through an injected ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"text":", so back it with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Keychain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"macOS sandbox & entitlements","anchor":"macOS-sandbox--entitlements","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"text":" uses the data-protection keychain, so it never raises","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a user prompt — no “Always Allow \/ Deny” dialog, no locked-keychain prompt, no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Touch ID \/ Face ID challenge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sandboxed"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" macOS app still needs a keychain entitlement, even when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not sharing items across an access group. Xcode supplies an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"application-identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" automatically for provisioning-profile–signed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds; otherwise add an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"xml"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Without it, the first ","type":"text"},{"code":"setValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fails with ","type":"text"},{"code":"errSecMissingEntitlement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"OSStatus","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" −34018). This is a build\/signing condition, not a runtime","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prompt. iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS need no extra entitlement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Tip","style":"tip","type":"aside"},{"level":3,"text":"Unsigned builds and test hosts","anchor":"Unsigned-builds-and-test-hosts","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A build made with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO"},{"text":" embeds no entitlements at all, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"text":" never reaches the binary and every write returns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"−34018. Test hosts and most CI invocations are built that way, which puts the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entitlement advice above out of reach: there is nothing to attach it to.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"text":" treats that as an environment condition rather than a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bug: it logs, returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":", and carries on. Reach for the returned value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where the app has something to fall back to.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let identity = keychain.deviceIdentity()   \/\/ usable even if nothing persisted"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/deviceIdentity(key:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" already works this way — a failed write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yields a session-local identity instead of a crash. Adopters do not need to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"detect XCTest and swap in a different store.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Adding a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"text":" entry has a cost worth weighing: it makes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app require a provisioning profile for any signed build, which breaks ad-hoc and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"local unsigned builds that otherwise run fine. Add it because you want the access","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group, not to silence −34018.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Encryption, accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and backup exclusion are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identical whichever entitlement you use — the access group only controls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"which of your own apps","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" can read an item, never third parties or the cloud.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For a private device ID, in order of strictness:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Most private:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" profile-signed build + "},{"code":"accessGroup: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", relying on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implicit "},{"code":"application-identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" group. No other app — even same-team —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS default; zero sharing surface."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Practically equivalent:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" a "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array whose only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entry is the team-prefixed bundle id (the snippet above). Use when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"profile-signed build isn’t available (unsigned local \/ CI dev). Only delta:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a same-team app you sign could also declare that string."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Intentional sharing only:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" a shared group string. The "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"becomes the default group for new items — never put a shared group first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for private data."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Device-Identity Pattern","anchor":"Device-Identity-Pattern","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The original motivation for ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" was apps without user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"auth that still want stable identity for analytics. Mint a UUID once with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/deviceIdentity(key:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" helper, hydrate into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"text":" at launch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and feed it to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceID"},{"text":" is also the stable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"feature-flag bucketing identity (the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceIDKeyPath"},{"text":"), so analytics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and A\/B exposure share one identity:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ `KVKey.deviceID` and `deviceIdentity()` ship with Swidux.","","\/\/ In Store.configured(), before constructing the store:","let kv = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")","let deviceID = kv.deviceIdentity()   \/\/ reads, or mints-and-persists, a stable UUID","","let initialState = AppState(deviceID: deviceID, \/* … *\/)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then in the analytics plugin wiring:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["AnalyticsPlugin(","    service: analytics,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, properties: { _ in [:] }),","    \/\/ …",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure-based ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userID"},{"text":" keypath runs on every dispatch, so the value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"must","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" live in state — never call into the Keychain from the closure. Hydrate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once; observe state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Type-safe Keys","anchor":"Type-safe-Keys","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare each key once on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference"},{"text":" so the value type travels with the name —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no magic strings at call sites:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == SortOrder {","    static let sortOrder = KVKey<SortOrder>(\"sortOrder\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let lastSeenVersion = KVKey<String>(\"lastSeenVersion\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then read and write through static-member literals. The compiler enforces","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that the value type matches what you declared:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let theme = store.value(.theme) ?? .system            \/\/ Theme?","store.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","store.setValue(.alphabetical, for: .sortOrder)","store.removeValue(for: .lastSeenVersion)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A typo or wrong type produces a compile error, not a silent miss at runtime.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Centralizing keys on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference"},{"text":" also gives you autocomplete and a single place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to audit your preference surface.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Wiring","anchor":"Wiring","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"text":"1. Add to your environment","anchor":"1-Add-to-your-environment","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct AppEnvironment: Sendable {","    var keyValue: any KeyValueStore","","    static func live() -> AppEnvironment {","        AppEnvironment(keyValue: UserDefaultsKeyValueStore())","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"2. Hydrate at startup","anchor":"2-Hydrate-at-startup","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read once into the initial state — never read mid-cycle from a reducer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension AppState {","    static func hydrated(from store: any KeyValueStore) -> AppState {","        AppState(","            theme: store.value(.theme) ?? .system,","            sortOrder: store.value(.sortOrder) ?? .alphabetical,","            lastSeenVersion: store.value(.lastSeenVersion)","        )","    }","}","","let env = AppEnvironment.live()","let store = AppStore.configured(state: .hydrated(from: env.keyValue), environment: env)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"3. Write from an effect","anchor":"3-Write-from-an-effect","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mutate state in the reducer, return an effect that writes the value:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["case .themeChanged(let theme):","    state.theme = theme","    return Effect { @Sendable _ in","        environment.keyValue.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no ","type":"text"},{"code":"do\/catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" does not throw —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder errors are programmer mistakes (e.g. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float.nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so the store logs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and triggers ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in DEBUG instead of forcing every effect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to handle an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it can’t act on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Testing","text":"Testing","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Inject ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and assert against the same instance:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Test","@MainActor","func themeChangePersists() async throws {","    let prefs = InMemoryKeyValueStore()","    let env = AppEnvironment(keyValue: prefs)","    let store = AppStore.configured(state: AppState(), environment: env)","","    try await confirmation(expectedCount: 1) { confirm in","        store.send(.themeChanged(.dark))","","        for _ in 0..<50 {","            if prefs.value(.theme) == .dark {","                confirm()","                break","            }","            try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(10))","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Simulate a relaunch.","    let rehydrated = AppState.hydrated(from: prefs)","    #expect(rehydrated.theme == .dark)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tests touching real ","type":"text"},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" should use a fresh per-test suite and tear","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it down explicitly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let suiteName = \"myapp.tests.\\(UUID().uuidString)\"","let defaults = UserDefaults(suiteName: suiteName)!","defer { defaults.removePersistentDomain(forName: suiteName) }","","let store = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore(suite: defaults)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Reads Are For Hydration","anchor":"Reads-Are-For-Hydration","type":"heading"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" mid-cycle (inside a reducer) is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anti-pattern. Reducers must be pure and synchronous; reads happen once at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" construction. After hydration, the value lives in state and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downstream code observes state, not the store.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":" itself is thread-safe, but a reducer reading while an effect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes creates ordering ambiguity. Hydrate, observe state, write through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effects — that’s the discipline.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Failure Modes","anchor":"Failure-Modes","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Missing key","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Provide a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default at the call site.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decode failure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and logs through ","type":"text"},{"code":"os.Logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(subsystem ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"swidux\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", category ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"kvstore\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). On startup, behaves identically","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to first launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encode failure"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — logged at the same subsystem\/category, then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fires in DEBUG so the bug surfaces during development.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Production builds log and continue; the in-memory state is unchanged. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API does not throw — there is no useful runtime recovery from inside an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effect, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would just hide the problem.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keychain unreachable"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — an unsigned build, a locked device, or a missing entitlement makes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes fail for reasons no caller can fix. These log and return ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; they do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" trap, because a test host built without code signing would otherwise crash on its first write. Malformed queries still assert in DEBUG. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore\/deviceIdentity(key:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" additionally distinguishes an unreadable item (locked keychain before first unlock, or an existing item that fails to decode) from a genuinely missing one: it only mints and persists a new identity when the item is confirmed absent, never when it merely couldn’t be read — reading an existing identity right after a reboot must not look like reinstalling the app. An unreadable item yields an unpersisted, session-only identity instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setValue"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeValue"},{"text":" return ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@discardableResult Bool"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store holds the intended state. Ignore it for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":", which has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reachability failure to report; check it for the Keychain wherever a fallback","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exists.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"@AppStorage Interop","anchor":"AppStorage-Interop","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There is none, by design. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" writes JSON-encoded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" blobs. SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only observes native primitive types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"URL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", raw ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Two parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation channels — Swidux state and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — would drift.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux state is the source of truth. Read once at hydration, then observe","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state through the store.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Schema Migration","anchor":"Schema-Migration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Out of scope for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". If a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shape changes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incompatibly, declare a new versioned key:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ before:","extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","\/\/ after a breaking shape change:","extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme.v2\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Old keys can be cleaned up at startup with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/removeValue(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(declare a tombstone ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of any value type — only the name is read).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/InMemoryKeyValueStore":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InMemoryKeyValueStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"InMemoryKeyValueStore","abstract":[{"text":"In-memory ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for tests.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"InMemoryKeyValueStore","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/doc